ere the attacker serves no job at either rate counts as not lower. Seed-bootstrap intervals are \const{95}\% paired percentile intervals from \const{9999} resamples (seed \const{0}), resampling seeds within each market; market $t$ intervals use \const{5} degrees of freedom. We call the replication prospective-exploratory: its plan was fixed and stamped before its markets existed, but it is not part of either registered test and changes no registered decision.
 
